  "source": "cft_golden/routines.py: divfull's and sqrtfull's instructions, relocated and specialised at the program's attribute; the math library's fragments, cft_golden/mathlib.py's, built at the program's format and attribute",
  "flags": "each runs in a quiet region and raises exactly its operation's flags: revision 8's flag control, QUIET, ENDQUIET and RAISE (docs/SEQUENCER.md R24); the math library's six also set the raised word's bit 7 where their in-lane test cannot decide the last bit, which marks the lane (R23's byte [7], STATUS[6]): its value is then the routine's best guess, which the definition replays (docs/LANGUAGE.md, \"A marked lane\")"
 },
